  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given an infinite binary tree called Funny&nbsp;Tree\\textbf{Funny Tree}Funny&nbsp;Tree. This tree has one vertex labeled with every positive integer, and the children of the vertex labeled iii are the vertices labeled 2i2i2i and 2i+12i+12i+1.\n\nThe first 151515 nodes of the tree are depicted in the image below.\n\n\n\nMathModel selects a node uuu and an integer NNN. Starting from node uuu, MathModel will repeatedly move to the parent node until he has either:\n\n\nVisited nnn nodes in total; or\nReached node 111, the root.\nThen, he calculates the sum of all nodes that he has visited.\n\nFor example, if MathModel selected u=6u=6u=6 and N=2N=2N=2, the path would be 6→36 \\to 36→3 with sum 999.\n\nIf he instead selected u=6u=6u=6 and any n≥3n\\ge 3n≥3, the path would be 6→3→16 \\to 3 \\to 16→3→1 with sum 101010.\n\nYou are given the movement parameter NNN, and the final sum obtained, XXX. Find any starting node uuu that's no larger than 101810^{18}1018, such that if MathModel starts at uuu and performs the process with parameter NNN, the resulting score will be exactly equal to XXX, or report that no such node exists.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains two space-separated integers XXX and NNN — the required sum and the movement parameter respectively.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case print a single line containing the answer: a possible starting node uuu (1≤u≤10181 \\le u \\le 10^{18}1≤u≤1018), or −1-1−1 if it does not exist.\n\n\nIf there are multiple possible starting nodes uuu that result in the sum XXX, you may output any of them.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1031 \\leq T \\leq 10^31≤T≤103",
      "1≤N,X≤10181 \\leq N, X \\leq 10^{18}1≤N,X≤1018"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "10\n9 2\n7 5\n10 2\n100 2\n100 4\n100 5\n5 5\n8 2\n7 2\n19999999989 100",
        "output": "6\n4\n7\n67\n54\n52\n-1\n-1\n5\n10000000000",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: A possible starting node is u=6u = 6u=6, which gives the sum 6+3=96+3 = 96+3=9.\nTest case 222: A possible starting node is u=4u = 4u=4, which gives the sum 4+2+1=74+2+1 = 74+2+1=7.\nNote that MathModel visited only 333 nodes even though N=5N=5N=5, because he stops after reaching node 111.\nTest case 777: There is no valid starting node uuu."
      }
    ]
